if the corresponding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line-type attribute is not dashed."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attributes let this be changed two ways."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element, such as a note or a notation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"orientation","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The orientation attribute indicates whether slurs and ties are overhand (tips down)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or underhand (tips up). This is distinct from the placement attribute used by any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation type."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierX","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point for one with a stop or continue type."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierY","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point for one with a stop or continue type."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierX2","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"continue type."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierY2","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"continue type."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierOffset","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur or tie"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a start type, or the incoming control point offset for one with a stop or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierOffset2","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX2"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltied\/init(id:kind:number:linekind:dashlength:spacelength:position:placement:orientation:bezierx:beziery:bezierx2:beziery2:bezieroffset:bezieroffset2:color:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/init(id:kind:number:lineKind:dashLength:spaceLength:position:placement:orientation:bezierX:bezierY:bezierX2:bezierY2:bezierOffset:bezierOffset2:color:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLTied","type":"c